---
title: TagGroup
description: Tags categorise content and can represent keywords, filters, or people.
category: Navigation
---

## Example

```jsx {% live=true %}
<TagGroup aria-label="Animals">
  <TagList>
    <Tag id="bilby">Bilby</Tag>
    <Tag id="kangaroo">Kangaroo</Tag>
    <Tag id="quokka">Quokka</Tag>
    <Tag id="echidna">Echidna</Tag>
  </TagList>
</TagGroup>
```

## Collections

`TagGroup` uses the React Aria Components collection API. Put static or
dynamic `Tag` elements inside an explicit `TagList`.

```jsx {% live=true %}
let items = [
  { id: 1, name: 'Bilby' },
  { id: 2, name: 'Kangaroo' },
  { id: 3, name: 'Quokka' },
  { id: 4, name: 'Echidna' },
];

return (
  <TagGroup aria-label="Animals">
    <TagList items={items}>
      {item => <Tag>{item.name}</Tag>}
    </TagList>
  </TagGroup>
);
```

## Slots

Icons and other content can be included in a tag. Provide `textValue` when
the children are not plain text.

```jsx {% live=true %}
<TagGroup label="Meal options">
  <TagList>
    <Tag id="healthy" textValue="Healthy">
      <Icon src={saladIcon} />
      <Text>Healthy</Text>
    </Tag>
    <Tag id="fast-food" textValue="Fast food">
      <Icon src={pizzaIcon} />
      <Text>Fast food</Text>
    </Tag>
    <Tag id="dessert" textValue="Dessert">
      <Icon src={dessertIcon} />
      <Text>Dessert</Text>
    </Tag>
  </TagList>
</TagGroup>
```

## Removing tags

Provide `onRemove` on `TagGroup`. The handler receives the set of tag IDs
to remove.

```jsx {% live=true %}
let [items, setItems] = React.useState([
  { id: 1, name: 'Bilby' },
  { id: 2, name: 'Kangaroo' },
  { id: 3, name: 'Quokka' },
]);

return (
  <TagGroup
    aria-label="Removable animals"
    onRemove={keys =>
      setItems(items => items.filter(item => !keys.has(item.id)))
    }
  >
    <TagList items={items}>
      {item => <Tag>{item.name}</Tag>}
    </TagList>
  </TagGroup>
);
```
